 Bakery                                              Time:  6:00 pm
Taken.


>eat pie
If you ate it in the dark, you'd probably make a mess all over yourself.


>examine table
A standard wooden table for customers to eat at.


>examine moon
It's nearly full and its craters form their familiar pattern.


>n

Closet
A small utility closet with a circuit breaker on the wall.  You can leave to the
south.


>examine breaker
Your standard circuit breaker, with two columns of labeled switches. Currently,
the switch marked "lights" is off.


>turn on breaker
You flip the switch and the overhead lights fill with an odd flickering glow.


>eat pie
Oh wow!  Everything seems so cosmic!

Inside Clockwork
You're walking up the teeth of a rotating gear to maintain your position.  Below
you it meshes with another gear.  Flickers of light bounce off the golden
spinning discs surrounding you in every direction.


>examine gear
The gears each appear to be about 5 meters in diameter, with large teeth that
serve as a steep staircase.  They're made of a shiny yellow metal, presumeably
the same substance that's in golden candy wrappers.


>u
You're already climbing the gear as fast as you can.


>put broom in gear
You wedge the broom between the teeth of the gears and they grind to a halt.

Last Custard Stand
There is a a roadside pie stand here.  A cardboard man holds up a sign
advertising custards for one dollars a piece.  He doesn't look too happy.


>examine me
You are wearing your bakery uniform and feel fine.


